      "id": 1,
      "text": "La Ronge began in 1904 as a fur trading post and meeting place, later diversifying after hunting declined.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Ronge"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the western shore of Lac La Ronge, adjacent to the provincial park and on the edge of the Canadian Shield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Ronge"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1782, Swiss fur trader Jean‑Étienne Waddens established a post on Lac La Ronge, later fatally wounded in a quarrel with Peter Pond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Ronge"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "La Ronge Wild Rice Corporation processes freshly harvested wild rice from local farmers each fall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Ronge"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Woodlands & Waterways Regional Visitor Centre, located in La Ronge, showcases the natural wonders and cultural treasures of northern Saskatchewan.",
